<title>COSTA RICA: Costa Rica reiterates 97-98 coffee crop forecast.</title>
<headline>Costa Rica reiterates 97-98 coffee crop forecast.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Costa Rica 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Costa Rica's 97-98 coffee crop will be around 3.2 million 46-kg bags compared to the 2.9 million quintals in 1996-1997, the executive director of the Costa Rican Coffee Institute said Monday.</p>
<p>Guillermo Canet, reiterating a previous institute crop prediction given at a tea and coffee symposium in Viena in June, said the forecast was for a better overall harvest. Cyclical reasons have also been given for the outlook.</p>
<p>((--Jose Loria, San Jose bureau +506 224-2949))</p>
